# Configure ConnectionStrings__IdentityDb and Jwt__Key/Jwt__Issuer/Jwt__Audience
# before starting the API. Jwt__Key must contain at least 32 UTF-8 bytes.
# Apply the Identity schema with EF migrations before sending requests.
# For example: dotnet ef database update --project Src\Modules\Identity\Kahrad.Pricing.Identity.Infrastructure --startup-project Src\Hosts\Kahrad.Pricing.Api --context IdentityDbContext
@Kahrad.Pricing.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5276
@accessToken = replace-with-access-token
@refreshToken = replace-with-refresh-token

### Password login
POST {{Kahrad.Pricing.Api_HostAddress}}/api/identity/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "replace-with-password"
}

### Refresh tokens
POST {{Kahrad.Pricing.Api_HostAddress}}/api/identity/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### List users (Admin or SuperAdmin)
GET {{Kahrad.Pricing.Api_HostAddress}}/api/users?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###
